From f39277a42450a9c4d5bf3298ca1fe08d64850c87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:51:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/41] libos/linux: Fail readv and writev with EINVAL when the
 lengths overflow

POSIX: readv and writev shall fail with [EINVAL] if "The sum of the
iov_len values in the iov array overflowed an ssize_t"; for writev
"no data shall be transferred". Linux shortens such a transfer (or
says EFAULT); add up the lengths first.
---
 libos/linux/local-uio.h | 65 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libos/linux/readv.c     | 14 ++++++---
 libos/linux/writev.c    | 14 ++++++---
 3 files changed, 85 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 libos/linux/local-uio.h

diff --git a/libos/linux/local-uio.h b/libos/linux/local-uio.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..89aeb6c62f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libos/linux/local-uio.h
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
